<title>USA: Clinton enlists 5 companies to help welfare reform.</title>
<headline>Clinton enlists 5 companies to help welfare reform.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton said on Tuesday that he had enlisted five companies to kick off a national effort to create jobs for former welfare recipients.</p>
<p>The five are: Sprint Corp, Monsanto Co, the United Parcel Service of America Inc, Grand Metropolitan Plc's Burger King and UAL Corp's United Airlines.</p>
<p>Clinton made the announcement in his State of the Union address to Congress and a national television audience.</p>
<p>&quot;Over the last four years, we moved a record 2-1/4 million people off the welfare rolls,&quot; the president said. &quot;Now we must act to meet a new goal: two million people off the welfare rolls by the year 2000.&quot;</p>
<p>He called for tax credits and other incentives for businesses that hire people off welfare.</p>
</text>
